---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConversionActions from '../components/ConversionActions.astro';
import InvestigationDeliverables from '../components/InvestigationDeliverables.astro';
import InvestigationFAQ from '../components/InvestigationFAQ.astro';
import Testimonial from '../components/Testimonial.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { pg14Facts } from '../data/facts';
---
<BaseLayout title="PostgreSQL Performance Consultant for RDS & Aurora | WalStack"
  description="Independent PostgreSQL engineer. I find why your RDS or Aurora database is slow or expensive and give you safe fixes. Start with a free snapshot review.">
  <header class="container hero intro">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">WalStack · PostgreSQL performance consultant · Kiran Sabne, Pune, India</p>
      <h1>Find what's slowing down production PostgreSQL.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I'm Kiran Sabne, an independent PostgreSQL performance engineer. When RDS, Aurora or self-managed Postgres gets slow or expensive, I find out why. I show you the evidence and give you a fix you can test safely.</p>
      <ConversionActions />
      <p class="small">Run one read-only script. Get 3 written findings within 2 business days. No database access needed.</p>
      <p class="trust">Read-only by default · Fixed prices · Refund if I find nothing you can act on</p>
    </div><Portrait />
  </header>
  <section><div class="container split"><h2>Sound familiar?</h2><div>
    <ul class="signal-list"><li>Pages or APIs slowed down after a release. Nobody can point to the query responsible.</li>
      <li>CPU or Aurora capacity spikes, even when traffic is steady and nothing has shipped.</li>
      <li>Your database bill grows faster than your user base.</li>
      <li>You're still on PostgreSQL 14. RDS standard support ends in February 2027.</li>
      <li>You have no dedicated DBA. The engineer who knows the database is busy shipping features.</li></ul>
    <p>If one of these is happening now, <a href="/snapshot">start with the free snapshot</a>.</p>
  </div></div></section>
  <section><div class="container"><h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol class="steps"><li><h3>Free snapshot</h3><p>You run one read-only script and send me the output. I reply with 3 written findings within 2 business days.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Investigation at a fixed price</h3><p>If you want to go further, I trace the slowdown using a read-only role. You can also run my scripts yourself.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Fix and verify</h3><p>You get the exact changes, what each one locks and how to undo it. I check the result 14 days later.</p></li></ol>
  </div></section>
  <section><div class="container offer split"><div><p class="eyebrow">The paid investigation</p>
    <h2><a href="/postgresql-performance-investigation">Postgres Slowdown Investigation</a></h2>
    <p class="price">$450</p><p>Founding price for my first 3 clients, then $750. Paid upfront.</p></div>
    <div><h3>What you get</h3><InvestigationDeliverables />
      <p>I deliver in 3 business days after I get access or your script output.</p>
      <p><strong>If I can't find at least one evidence-backed improvement, you get a full refund.</strong></p>
      <ConversionActions primary="Start with a free snapshot" call="Book a call" />
    </div></div></section>
  <section><div class="container split"><h2>Upgrading off PostgreSQL 14?</h2><div>
    <p>RDS standard support ends on 28 February 2027. From 1 March, AWS charges extra for eligible instances that stay on 14 with Extended Support enabled. <a href={pg14Facts.awsSource}>AWS release calendar</a>.</p>
    <p>I check what could break and record how your busiest queries run today. You get a plan to compare performance after the upgrade and roll back if needed.</p>
    <p><a href="/postgresql-upgrade-readiness">PostgreSQL Upgrade Readiness</a> · <strong>{site.upgradeOffer.display}</strong></p>
    <a class="button" data-track="book_call_click" href={site.bookingUrl}>Ask about your upgrade</a>
  </div></div></section>
  <section><div class="container split"><h2>What you'll receive</h2><div>
    <p><a href="/sample-report" data-track="sample_report_click">See a sample report</a>. I built it on a demo database. It contains no client results.</p>
    <p><a href="/case-studies">Lab case studies</a>. I reproduced these problems on generated data. All measurements come from the lab.</p>
    <p>I built <a href={site.planReaderUrl} data-track="planreader_click">PlanReader</a> to read database execution plans. I also built <a href={site.extensionUrl}>pg_stat_index_queries</a>, an experimental open-source PostgreSQL extension.</p>
    <p>WalStack is <a href={site.directoryUrl}>listed in PostgreSQL.org's Professional Services directory</a>.</p>
  </div></div></section>
  <Testimonial />
  <section><div class="container split"><h2>About me</h2><div>
    <p>I'm Kiran Sabne. I've spent about 8 years in database and backend engineering, including about 6 with PostgreSQL in production.</p>
    <p>I've worked on RDS and Aurora, moved and partitioned large tables, built pipelines that copy database changes, and handled major upgrades.</p>
    <p>I work alone and take a few engagements each month. From Pune, India, I work asynchronously and overlap with US mornings and UK/EU afternoons.</p>
    <p><a href={site.linkedinUrl}>LinkedIn</a> · <a href={site.githubUrl}>GitHub</a> · <a href="/about">More about me</a></p>
  </div></div></section>
  <section><div class="container split"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><InvestigationFAQ /></div></section>
  <section><div class="container offer"><h2>Something slow right now? Send me a snapshot.</h2><ConversionActions /></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
